      ],
      "sheet_exponents_and_signs": [
        [
          1,
          -1
        ],
        [
          -1,
          1
        ]
      ]
    }
  ],
  "law": "The exponents are multiplied by k. With unit k and M>=3 the +/-k cells are distinct. At each chosen port they each have squared mass 1/8. In the product record the two opposite-sheet orders have total mass 2/64=1/32 per port iff fold_M(2k)=2; otherwise the contribution is zero. Thus the full probability is 1/16 or zero.",
  "general_unit_classification": "For M>=5 this is equivalent to 2k=+/-2 mod M, or k=+/-1 mod M/gcd(2,M). At odd M only +/-1 pass. At M=2 mod 4 only +/-1 are units in that class; at M divisible by 4, +/-1+M/2 also pass, with overlaps at M=4.",
